From 5d3c205c759adc02cf910abcc532a3fbea555234 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 08:37:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 30/58] e2_guards: executable graph-profile and
 breakable-cudagraph guards

New vllm/v1/e2_guards.py, called from the target and MTP constructors on every
rank before profiling or capture: the breakable-cudagraph pin is asserted
(three readings of the switch), a graph profile that cannot execute on v0.30.0
is refused, and VLLM_E2_EXPECTED_CUDAGRAPH_MODE is checked by name. Tests
cover the drafter. An inert knob is no longer hashed into the cache key.
